From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0182-no-mesh-pipelines-for-skipped-draws.patch

Source: 0182-no-mesh-pipelines-for-skipped-draws.patch
Core patch, for tools/eglantine-patches after 0181. Ours, no source to credit.

EDEN_NX2_NO_MESH drops a task/mesh draw only after CurrentGraphicsPipeline has built its pipeline.
So every session translates these pipelines on the GPU thread and hands them to the driver, for
draws that are thrown away. They are never stored either (next patch), so it happens again each
run. That is the burst on entering the forest:

  run 57: 83 built in the first 10 s, all 83 task/mesh, 1917 ms
  run 58: 98, 95 task/mesh, 1979 ms
  run 61: 106, 103 task/mesh, 2195 ms
  run 62: 103, all 103 task/mesh, 2198 ms; at least 165 task/mesh in the session, 4088 ms of 5802 ms

(A build counts as task/mesh when "Task program"/"Mesh program" lines come before it in the log.
Those lines stop after 256, so later ones are not counted: run 62's 165 is a floor.)

Switch: EDEN_NX2_NO_MESH_BUILD=1, together with EDEN_NX2_NO_MESH. Default off, the old behaviour.
It does nothing with EDEN_NX2_NO_MESH_FILE, which can turn those draws back on and then needs the
pipelines, and nothing without EDEN_NX2_NO_MESH.

With it, PrepareDraw leaves before the lookup: no shader refresh, no key, no pipeline. The draw
ends as before: nothing recorded, submitted stays false, and the same "Draw skipped
(EDEN_NX2_NO_MESH)" line, which run-report.py counts. Dirty::Shaders stays set, so the next draw
refreshes the shaders. IsMeshEnabled on a native program is what makes GraphicsEnvironment give
the Task/Mesh stage, so these are the draws IsMeshPipeline would have dropped.

One order changes: TryNx2IndirectReset ran before the old drop and does not run now. It only
matches one 11-instruction vertex program, which would not be bound with mesh mode on. Read, not
run.

Memory: expected to give back driver memory (the comment in EvictUnusedPipelines says about 0.45 MB
a pipeline, measured on another title). Not measured. Not run on a console. Syntax checked with
clang (stubs for the SDK).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

